      "body": "normalize_partition_spec in torchtitan/distributed/spmd_types.py overwrote entries[dim] instead of accumulating into it, so when two mesh axes independently shard the same tensor dimension (a supported configuration, e.g. PartitionSpec((DP, CP))), only the last axis survived and the other was silently dropped from the synthesized spec used by the shard-order validator.\n\nFix\n\nChanged entries[dim] = (MeshAxisName(axis_name),) to entries[dim] = entries[dim] + (MeshAxisName(axis_name),) so all axes sharding a given dim are preserved, in order.\n\nTest plan\n\nIsolated the function’s logic with stub types (the real spmd_types package is internal/unavailable) and confirmed: before the fix, two axes (dp, cp) both sharding dim 0 collapsed to (('cp',), ()) — dp lost; after the fix, (('dp', 'cp'), ()) — both preserved in insertion order. Verified the patched file parses correctly.",
